# Generic synthesis for area and logic-depth evidence.
#
# No liberty file exists in an open-source flow, so this cannot produce signed
# timing.  What it CAN produce is the number that decides whether 1 GHz is
# plausible at all: the longest combinational path in LOGIC LEVELS.  At 1 GHz in
# a modern node the budget is roughly 30-40 levels of simple gates.
#
# dfflegalize forces every flop to a plain $_DFF_P_ first.  Without it, flops
# with clock enables ($_DFFE_PP_) are not recognised by `ltp -noff`, every enable
# feedback Q->mux->D reads as a combinational cycle, and the report is a wall of
# spurious "Detected loop" warnings.  `check -assert` (check.ys) is the
# authoritative loop test and it passes.
read_verilog -sv build/slice.v
hierarchy -top hbm4_pc_slice
proc; opt; fsm; opt; memory; opt
# FLATTEN before any path analysis.  Unflattened, ltp treats each submodule
# instance as a black box in which every input reaches every output, so any two
# blocks that feed one another read as a combinational cycle even when the real
# path between them is registered.  That is where 185 spurious "Detected loop"
# warnings came from -- not from the design.  check.ys is the authoritative
# loop test and it passes.
flatten; opt
techmap; opt
dfflegalize -cell $_DFF_P_ x
abc -g simple
opt_clean
tee -o rpt/stat.txt stat
tee -o rpt/ltp.txt ltp -noff
